  "national": {
    "$comment": "German profiles: gematik ePA and KBV MIO (#1172, step 2 of discussion #1169), and the MII Kerndatensatz (core data set) the university hospitals' data integration centres deliver for research. eehrxfCounterpart names the EEHRxF profile a German profile covers the same ground as. build.py writes the guides marked onPage to neo4j/register-national-profiles.cypher and ui/public/mock/eehrxf_national.json, never to the EEHRxF outputs; the ePA and MIO guides stay in the report only, because real organisation names are kept out of the default build's graph and mocks (fictional organisation policy, .claude/rules/code-style.md). Not EEHRxF: validate.py writes their results to the report's national section, and /eehrxf shows the onPage ones in a section of their own, never counted as EEHRxF coverage. Each IG is validated in a run of its own, because each pins other versions of the HL7 Europe and German base packages than the EEHRxF run does. Mapped by what we produce: lab Observation, DiagnosticReport and Bundle to the lab guides, MedicationRequest to the ePA prescription profile, and Patient, Condition, Procedure, Encounter, MedicationRequest and MedicationStatement to the MII modules Person, Diagnose, Prozedur, Fall and Medikation. Versions checked on the date and at the URL each IG records.",
